    "q-27729": {
      "dom_id": "step-q27729",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Solve the equation ${log}_{8}⁡({x}^{2}+19x)={log}_{8}⁡(10x-8).$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡({x}^{2}+19x) & ={log}_{8}⁡(10x-8) \\\\ {x}^{2}+19x & =10x-8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x+8) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=-1$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡({x}^{2}+19x) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(10x-8) \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡((-1)^{2}+19(-1)) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(10(-1)-8) \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡(-18) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(-18)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not valid because ${log}_{8}⁡(-18)$ is undefined. Therefore, $x=-1$ is not a valid solution.\n\n- Substituting $x=-8$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡({x}^{2}+19x) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(10x-8) \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡((-8)^{2}+19(-8)) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(10(-8)-8) \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡(-88) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{8}⁡(-88)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not valid because ${log}_{8}⁡(-88)$ is undefined. Therefore, $x=-8$ is not a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"No solutions.\"",
